--- !u!114 &933713811
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 933713806}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5ed11cbb11006e046a195f7f82b8ae58, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogueManager: {fileID: 1705817792}
  conversation:
  - speakerName: Leon
    sentenceText: Dr. Almeda? One of the workers inside told me you were out here.
      I am with ARPHIS. They said you are the main historian for the archives.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Dr. Almeda
    sentenceText: Finally. I have been watching the shadows since the alarms went
      off. I have worked in these halls for thirty years, and I never thought I would
      see the day our history was treated like common boxes.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Leon
    sentenceText: "The team at the TOC said the thieves were very neat and careful.
      They knew exactly what to take\u2014and what to delete from the computers."
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Dr. Almeda
    sentenceText: They were very careful with the computer files, yes. But they did
      not think about those of us who still keep paper records. I managed to grab
      the master file for the Paete collection before they could lock down the office
      wing.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Leon
    sentenceText: I found a broken piece of Baticulin wood inside. The Professor
      said it breaks easily when dry, which is why it broke when it was dropped.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Dr. Almeda
    sentenceText: He is right. Baticulin is loved by Paete carvers for its details,
      but it breaks very easily. Seeing it broken on the floor is heartbreaking.
      In fact, I was right there inside the museum when the theft happened.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Leon
    sentenceText: You were inside?
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Dr. Almeda
    sentenceText: Yes, I quickly hid in the dark corners of the gallery so they would
      not see me. From my hiding spot, I watched them take the main diorama. Since
      it was too big to carry out whole, I heard them plan to break it into five
      pieces to fit into their bags. Their leader also ordered them to scatter cheap,
      fake copies across the park grounds to trick our security team.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Leon
    sentenceText: So the real fragments are hidden among fakes to trick us.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Dr. Almeda
    sentenceText: "This is the complete registry. It lists every single Paete item
      brought to the museum, starting from the very first diorama\u2014the Cagayan
      Valley piece\u2014up until the present day. It holds the exact wood details
      and information about the old carving tools they tried to erase."
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 537648405}
  - speakerName: Leon
    sentenceText: This is more than a list. This is a map of the entire collection.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Dr. Almeda
    sentenceText: Exactly. It contains deep details about Diorama 1, explaining the
      exact crude tools that the early carvers used to shape it. It notes the roughness
      of the wood, the uneven lines, and the special markings left by those old tools.
      Use this information as your guide. It foreshadows the exact wood textures
      and tool marks you need to look for. Study it well so you can tell the real
      fragments apart from the fakes when you are out there.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  triggerTabletNotificationOnEnd: 1
  requiresPreviousNPCDone: 1
  preRequisiteNPC: {fileID: 0}
