--- !u!114 &1241623299
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1241623295}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5ed11cbb11006e046a195f7f82b8ae58, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogueManager: {fileID: 1705817792}
  conversation:
  - speakerName: Leon
    sentenceText: "Barragan. My scanner just turned on with five different signatures
      around the area. What am I looking at? The diorama is in pieces\u2014how is
      it still sending a signal?"
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Rex Barragan
    sentenceText: That is our tracking system at work. Every high-value item in the
      Ayala collection has tiny trackers hidden inside the wood grain from when we
      preserved them.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Leon
    sentenceText: Even if the item is broken into pieces? I am getting signals from
      all over the maintenance area and the garden.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Rex Barragan
    sentenceText: "Exactly. As long as a broken diorama piece is larger than a few
      centimeters, the tracker stays active. It was made for situations just like
      this\u2014a messy escape. The thieves were in such a hurry that they did not
      know they were carrying a live signal."
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Leon
    sentenceText: If we can see them, why have your men not picked up the pieces
      yet?
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Rex Barragan
    sentenceText: Look at the map. The signals are mixed up with 'dead zones' in
      the maintenance pathways and the Service Alley. The thieves set up their own
      guards, and they are using signal jammers to create fake signals. My computer
      can tell you where the signals are, but we do not know which ones are the real
      Cagayan Valley fragments and which ones are fake blocks left to slow us down.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Leon
    sentenceText: That is where Dr. Almeda's guide comes in. I will use the GPS signals
      to find the locations, but I will use the registry information about the old
      carving tools and wood grains to check each diorama fragment before I pick
      it up.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  - speakerName: Rex Barragan
    sentenceText: Stay sharp, Investigator. The Service Alley has a lot of enemies.
      They know we are tracking them, and they are waiting for us to move. I have
      sent the live coordinates to your mini-map. Good luck.
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  triggerTabletNotificationOnEnd: 0
  requiresPreviousNPCDone: 1
  preRequisiteNPC: {fileID: 933713811}
  lockedFallbackConversation:
  - speakerName: Rex Barragan
    sentenceText: Talk to Dr. Almeda first
    documentPanelToShow: {fileID: 0}
  isPhoneCaller: 0
  callerName: HQ Dispatch
  callerPhoneNumber: 09XX-XXX-XXXX
  phoneCallerNameText: {fileID: 0}
  phoneCallerNumberText: {fileID: 0}
  phoneProfileImageDisplay: {fileID: 0}
  callerProfileSprite: {fileID: 0}
  hasCompletedConversation: 0
